<BaseLayout title="christopher joy — researcher">
  <div class="page-header">
    <h1>christopher j. joy</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">researcher &middot; consultant &middot; economics &amp; data</p>
  </div>
  <hr class="rule-accent" />

  <p>
    I'm Christopher — an economic researcher and consultant at Allegheny
    Economic Research, where I work on labor market dynamics, macroeconomic
    forecasting, and regional economic development across Western Pennsylvania.
    My day-to-day runs from validating and analyzing labor and employment data
    to building the databases and dashboards that turn it into something
    decision-makers can use. I work primarily in Stata, R, Python, and SQL.
  </p>

  <p>
    Alongside the applied work, my research interests center on developing
    economies, with a particular focus on Southeast Asia — female empowerment
    and poverty reduction, the region's political economies, and state-society
    relations. I've spent significant portions of the last decade in Southeast
    Asia and speak Vietnamese, Indonesian, and Thai.
  </p>

